HOW TO READ THIS LOG
  Items: C = CAT, D = DOG. Lights: 0 = OFF, 1 = ON. A world line 'CD > 10 > C!D' means guessers
  hold CAT, DOG; the lights are S0 ON, S1 OFF; G0 says DOG (wrong, marked !) and G1 says DOG.
  x0, x1, ... are the guessers' items. Success = reaching this graph's oracle reward.
  Families: tracking = every active light relays one item and as many items as possible are relayed;
  partial tracking = relays only, but fewer items; XOR-type = relays plus parity lights;
  nonlinear = at least one light combines items (AND/OR, majority, ...); silent = constant lights.
